GTKDialog development topics
============================

- Preserve the existing widget-initialization order until dependencies between
  widgets are explicitly modelled and covered by ordering regressions. Changing
  this order can alter synchronous actions in existing applications.

- Keep the legacy <chooser> and <gvim> tags compatible. They remain supported
  for existing applications, but should not be redesigned without compatibility
  evidence.

- Extend dedicated attributes only where GTK+ 2 constructor arguments, child
  packing, internal helper widgets or non-string property types cannot use the
  generic writable-property path documented in doc/reference/syntax.html.

- Bring the introductory Texinfo manual to feature parity with the maintained
  HTML reference. The HTML pages are the authoritative user documentation in
  the meantime.
